<h2>Why now</h2>

<p>The commercial opportunity is changing.</p>

<p>China extended zero-tariff treatment to imports from all African countries with diplomatic relations with Beijing on 1 May 2026 (<a href="https://english.news.cn/20260501/4a61884b19384e9995c54ba065ca32c5/c.html" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Xinhua, 1 May 2026</a>).</p>

<p>Tariffs are only one part of market access. Exporters still need to understand buyer preferences, product standards, food-safety requirements, packaging, documentation, logistics and distribution. Buyers need reliable suppliers who can deliver the right product, quality, volume and traceability.</p>

<p>The summit is designed to make those conversations easier and more direct.</p>

